A cafeteria totals lunch trays per station with this fragment:
int[][] trays = {{2, 5}, {1, 4}, {3, 0}};
int total = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < trays.length; r++) { for (int c = 0; c < trays[r].length; c++) { total += trays[r][c]; } }
System.out.println(total);
What value is printed?

A greenhouse controller combines two sensor cells with this fragment:
int[][] g = {{7, 8, 9}, {4, 5, 6}};
System.out.println(g[1][0] + g[0][2]);
What value is printed?

An aquarium monitor crashes on this setup:
int[][] m = new int[3][4];
m[3][0] = 5;
Which statement identifies the fault?

A farm stand totals Saturday sales from row 2 with this fragment:
int[][] sales = {{5, 1}, {2, 6}, {4, 3}};
System.out.println(sales[2][0] + sales[2][1]);
What value is printed?

A census tool must count every cell of a possibly uneven grid:
int n = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) { for (int c = 0; _____; c++) { n++; } }
Which guard belongs in the blank?

