A freezer log hunts the warmest reading, yet prints 0 on this data:
int[][] p = {{-4, -9}, {-2, -7}};
int best = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < p.length; r++) { for (int c = 0; c < p[r].length; c++) { if (p[r][c] > best) { best = p[r][c]; } } }
System.out.println(best);
Which statement identifies the fault? The true warmest reading is -2.

A chess club counts unique board pairings with this fragment:
int pairs = 0;
for (int r = 0; r < 6; r++) { for (int c = r + 1; c < 6; c++) { pairs++; } }
System.out.println(pairs);
What integer is printed?
